Common Network Ports and Security

Purpose

This document identifies common network ports, their services, and basic security considerations.

Port| Service| Purpose| Security Consideration
22| SSH| Remote administration| Restrict access and use strong authentication
53| DNS| Resolves domain names| Monitor suspicious DNS activity
80| HTTP| Web communication| Prefer HTTPS for sensitive traffic
443| HTTPS| Encrypted web communication| Maintain secure TLS configuration

Key Observation

An open port does not automatically indicate a vulnerability. Security depends on the service, configuration, exposure, and access controls.

Practical Limitations

This is a reference-based study. No live network scan was conducted.

Conclusion

Understanding common ports helps cybersecurity professionals assess network services and identify potential security risks.
